<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Document</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./style/style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style/faq.css">
    <link
      rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"
    />
</head>
<body>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%- include('partials/header') %>
    <main>
      <section class="articles">
        <h1>FAQ</h1>
        <article>
          <h2>What is the minimum age to attend the event?</h2>
          <p>
            You must be at least 18 years old to enter. No exceptions. 
            Make sure you are 18 or older on the day of the event.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>
            Do I need to show ID at the entrance?
          </h2>
          <p>
            Yes, you must show a valid ID to get in. Even if you look older than 18, staff may ask to see it. 
            Accepted IDs include a passport, ID card, or driver’s license.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Are lockers available at the event?</h2>
          <p>
            Yes, lockers are provided so you can safely store your personal belongings. 
            We recommend using a locker for valuables instead of carrying them with you.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>What time do the doors open and close?</h2>
          <p>
            The opening and closing times are different for each edition of the event. 
            Check the specific event page on our website or our social media channels before attending.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Does my ticket need to be in my name?</h2>
          <p>
            No, tickets for CENDO are not personal. The name on the ticket does not need to match the person attending.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>I bought tickets for the wrong event. Can I exchange them?</h2>
          <p>
            Unfortunately, tickets cannot be exchanged for a different edition. 
            You can resell your ticket safely through TicketSwap.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>
            Can I leave the venue and return later?
          </h2>
          <p>
            No, once you leave the venue, your ticket will no longer be valid. You cannot re-enter with the same ticket.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>What can I bring, and what is not allowed?</h2>
          <p>
            To keep everyone safe, the following items are not allowed at the event: <br>
            <br>
            - Hard drugs, nitrous oxide, pre-rolled joints (max 5 g of cannabis/hash is allowed if not pre-rolled) <br>
            <br>
            - Outside food and drinks (including alcohol) <br>
            <br>
            - Glass, cans, and plastic bottles <br>
            <br>
            - Umbrellas, selfie sticks, confetti, graffiti, laser pointers, and candles <br>
            <br>
            - Advertising materials such as stickers <br>
            <br>
            - Weapons, fireworks, or anything that could be used as a weapon <br>
            <br>
            - Other items that are similar to the above <br>
            <br>
            If you are unsure about an item, it’s best to leave it at home.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>Where can I see the timetable?</h2>
          <p>
            The timetable is shared before the event on our Instagram stories and posts. 
            During the event, it is also displayed on posters at the venue.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>I lost something during the event. What should I do?</h2>
          <p>
            If you lost an item, contact us within 4 weeks after the event via email or DM on Instagram. 
            Include the edition of the event and a detailed description of the lost item.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>How can I contact the organizers?</h2>
          <p>
            You can reach us via email or by sending a DM on Instagram. We try to reply as quickly as possible, 
            but please note that messages may take longer around the time of an event.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article>
          <h2>What are the rules at CENDO?</h2>
          <p>
            By entering the event, you agree to follow our rules. 
            These rules are in place to keep everyone safe and ensure a positive experience. This includes: <br>
            <br>
            - Respecting staff and other attendees <br>
            <br>
            - Following instructions from staff <br>
            <br>
            - Not bringing drugs or weapons <br>
            <br>
            - Following all safety regulations <br>
            <br>
            The full house rules can be found on our website.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
    <script src="/js/faq.js" defer></script>
  </body>
</html>
